# Regression test placeholder: E043 ResourceLimitExceeded is not yet triggerable
# This test documents that E043 exists in the error taxonomy but cannot be triggered
# via corpus tests because no resource limits are currently enforced beyond depth
# limits (which use E040/E041).
#
# BACKGROUND: E043 was added in Cycle #40 (2026-04-27) for resource-guard errors,
# but the triggering code paths (MAX_COLLECT_SIZE, MAX_STRING_SIZE) are enforced
# only in unit tests where they can be set to small values. Corpus tests cannot
# configure these limits, so E043 remains untestable here.
#
# NOTE: This is NOT an error test (expected output is successful evaluation).
# It was moved from tests/corpus/eval/errors/ where it didn't belong.

# Create a small dict (does NOT trigger E043)
[large: [a: 1  b: 2  c: 3]]
===
Dict({"large": Dict({"a": Int(1), "b": Int(2), "c": Int(3)})})
